# Warpgate + Infisical credential broker appliance

This appliance is the credential-bearing network boundary for MCP and other agents.

## SSH

Warpgate terminates the client SSH session and opens the target-side SSH session itself. Target passwords or private keys are resolved from Infisical just in time by the Warpgate process and are never returned to the MCP appliance.

## HTTP / HTTPS / REST

Infisical Agent Proxy listens on port 17322 and acts as a forward HTTP/HTTPS MITM proxy. Proxied services and injection rules are defined in Infisical. The proxy obtains the real API credential and attaches it at the network boundary; MCP receives only the upstream response.

The secure default is `unmatched-host=block`, so the proxy is an allow-listed egress path rather than a generic Internet proxy.

## Identity separation

Use two least-privilege Infisical machine identities:

- `INFISICAL_SSH_CLIENT_ID` with read access only to SSH target secrets used by Warpgate.
- `INFISICAL_AGENT_PROXY_CLIENT_ID` with Agent Proxy/proxied-service permissions and access to only the brokered HTTP credentials.

Their Universal Auth client secrets live only on this appliance as root-only Docker secret files:

- `/docker/warpgate/infisical-ssh-client-secret`
- `/docker/warpgate/infisical-agent-proxy-client-secret`

MCP should use its own short-lived/scoped agent identity when connecting to Agent Proxy. It should not be able to read the service secrets that the proxy brokers.

## Persistent state

Warpgate state lives under `/docker/warpgate/data`. Target records contain only Infisical references, not target passwords or private keys.
